{"at":"2026-10-21T14:37:16.449029Z","event":"agent_commit","task_id":"investigate","role":"solo","output":{"summary":"A deploy of orders-service v2.15.0 at 13:31 UTC introduced a new order amendment endpoint. Starting at 13:33 UTC the service threw NullPointerExceptions in AmendOrderHandler.validate because order.limitPrice was null, causing 500 responses that propagated to edge-gateway. Error-rate metric spiked while CPU, memory, DB pool and latency stayed normal. No config, flag, secret or infra changes occurred in the window. Root cause is a code regression in the newly added handler.","observations":[{"statement":"orders-service v2.15.0 deployed (add order amendment endpoint) at 2026-10-05T13:31:20Z","artifacts":["chg:2501"],"service":"orders-service","key":"F1"},{"statement":"orders-service logs show NullPointerException: order.limitPrice is null in AmendOrderHandler.validate (PATCH /v1/orders) – 413 occurrences, first at 13:33:01Z","artifacts":["log:0953dd5b47dc"],"service":"orders-service","key":"F2"},{"statement":"edge-gateway logs show upstream orders-service returned 500 on /v1/orders – 379 occurrences, first at 13:34:05Z","artifacts":["log:a41f996d606e"],"service":"edge-gateway","key":"F3"},{"statement":"orders-service error_rate metric rose from baseline 0.0021 to peak 0.0663 (mean 0.0185) between 13:31‑13:58Z","artifacts":["metric:orders-service/error_rate"],"service":"orders-service","key":"F4"},{"statement":"orders-service CPU, memory, DB pool usage, latency_p99 and RPS remained within normal bounds during the same window","artifacts":["metric:orders-service/cpu_util","metric:orders-service/mem_util","metric:orders-service/db_pool_in_use","metric:orders-service/latency_p99_ms","metric:orders-service/rps"],"service":"orders-service","key":"F5"}],"assumptions":[{"statement":"Customer edit action maps to PATCH /v1/orders (the amendment endpoint added in v2.15.0)","reason":"Reported symptom is “changing price or quantity of an open order” and the new endp